  "narration": "Your next shopping trip might not be done by you,\nbecause Meta just built an AI that buys things for you.\nFollow the channel, because the feed won't show us to you twice,\nand we unpack one AI update like this every day.\nIt's called Muse, launched in September in the US.\nYou tell it what you need, a gift, a jacket, a new charger,\nand it searches stores like Walmart, Best Buy and Gap,\nfills the cart, then asks you to approve before it pays.\nAnd now every store has to decide whether to let AI shoppers in.\nShopify is building checkouts for them,\nbut Amazon has blocked Muse from its site.\nSo a store that shuts the door could lose your sale,\nbecause your AI buys from one that lets it in.\nIn other words, a store's next customer may be an AI.\nBefore you hand it your card, check two things,\nwhat it can buy without asking, and where it's allowed to shop.\nWould you let an AI do your shopping?\nBecause your next shopping trip might not be done by you.\n",
